{"Background": ("Cecilia Reyes grew up in a tough neighborhood in the Bronx. From an early age, she aspired to become a doctor, motivated by the loss of her father to violent crime. When her mutant powers emerged, she was forced to confront the reality that her abilities might place her in danger—or worse, make her a target. Initially rejecting any notion of superheroics, she strove to serve her community as a physician, hoping that alone would be enough to make a difference.")}

{"Description": ("In recent months, after various encounters with the X-Men, Cecilia has embraced a more balanced life between hospital shifts and field missions. She remains committed to her patients, often pulling back-to-back shifts in the ER, then transitioning into Forcefield mode when a crisis emerges. She is more at peace with her dual role now, combining her medical expertise and mutant powers to protect others. Yet, her guarded demeanor persists; she shares little about her inner turmoil and focuses solely on the well-being of those around her.")}

